# UI/UX Contract

## Component Boundaries

- UI primitives must live in `src/components/ui/**`.
- Domain components must live in feature-specific folders.
- Do not duplicate shared primitives without strong justification.

## Required States

All user-facing screens and major data sections must support:
- loading state
- empty state
- error state

Mutations should also expose:
- pending or disabled state
- success or failure feedback when appropriate

## Upgrade-Required UX

When an action is blocked by plan limits:
- clearly explain the reason
- show the relevant limit and current usage when possible
- provide a single clear CTA to upgrade or manage billing/settings

## Sensitive Data Rules

The UI must never expose:
- cross-tenant data
- raw secrets
- raw tokens
- internal-only metadata
- internal IDs unless operationally necessary

## UX Consistency Rules

- Keep destructive actions explicit.
- Do not rely on client-only permission logic as the source of truth.
- Prefer server-derived gating and visibility decisions.
- Reuse shared UI patterns before creating new ones.

